     "field": "definition",
     "severity": "Medium",
     "issue": "Calls the passive 70V attenuator a 'L-pad attenuator'. Web-verified via AtlasIED 70-Volt Rules and Parts-Express/electronics-tutorials: passive 70V distributed-line volume controls are predominantly autotransformer (autoformer) types; a purely resistive L-pad cannot sit directly on a 70V line (it dissipates the load current as heat and overheats). 'L-pad' is the resistive low-impedance-speaker device, not the standard 70V attenuator.",
     "suggestion": "Change to '...a passive 70V autotransformer (autoformer) attenuator or a low-voltage/digital controller...'. Reserve 'L-pad' for resistive attenuation on low-impedance speaker lines."
